= Spiritus Myristicae
{parent=Pharmaceutical preparation}
{c}

Historical formulation name; composition is identified by pharmacopoeial edition.

= Spiritus Aetheris Nitrosi
{parent=Pharmaceutical preparation}
{c}

= Nitrous ether spirit
{synonym}

A historical alcoholic preparation containing nitrous ether; its composition is edition-specific.

= Proof spirit
{parent=Pharmaceutical preparation}

Historical aqueous <ethanol> of specified proof strength; it is not synonymous with <rectified spirit>.

= Rectified spirit
{parent=Pharmaceutical preparation}

Historical concentrated aqueous <ethanol> used as a pharmaceutical solvent; its specified strength depends on the applicable standard.

= Maceration
{parent=Pharmaceutical preparation}

Extraction by allowing divided material to stand in contact with a solvent; distinguished from passing fresh solvent through a packed bed in <percolation>.

= Liquid extract
{parent=Pharmaceutical preparation}

An extracted medicinal preparation supplied as a liquid of specified strength. The name alone does not impose a universal ratio of starting material to final liquid.

= Infusion
{parent=Pharmaceutical preparation}

A preparation obtained by allowing medicinal material to stand in a solvent for a specified time, at the prescribed <temperature>, then straining or filtering.

= Decoction
{parent=Pharmaceutical preparation}

A preparation made by boiling medicinal material in a liquid, followed by the specified separation and volume adjustment. Suitability depends on the <solubility> and heat stability of the desired constituents.

= Bismuth preparation
{parent=Pharmaceutical preparation}

= Iron preparation
{parent=Pharmaceutical preparation}

A medicinal article containing <iron>; a historical list includes chemically and pharmacologically distinct materials.

